 a hands-on manual for DIY restorers
作者：Alex Bealer
出版社：Countrywood News
A comprehensive guide to repairing and restoring a wooden chair, suitable for DIY enthusiasts and professionals. This book provides detailed instructions and photographs to guide the reader through the repair and restoration process, from assessing the chair's condition to reassembling the finished project. Topics covered include: assessing the chair's condition, disassembling the chair, repairing and replacing broken or damaged parts, refinishing and finishing, and reassembling the chair.
Alex Bealer has been a woodworking expert for over 30 years and has written several books on woodworking and restoration. He has also taught woodworking classes and workshops and has contributed to various woodworking magazines.
This book is an excellent resource for anyone looking for a step-by-step guide to repairing a wooden chair. The author, Alex Bealer, is a well-known expert in the field of woodworking and restoration, and his instructions are clear and easy to follow. The book includes detailed photographs and diagrams to help readers